#
# The LeakSanitizer suppressions for the daemon (build_test.sh --asan).
#
# A suppression names an allocation that is deliberately never freed: a
# boot-time snapshot, a registry that lives until the process exits. Each
# entry says why it is not a leak, and points at the allocation site. An
# entry that is not needed any more is removed: the sanitizer's report
# names the stack, and the run fails on a report that has no entry here.
#
# The format is LeakSanitizer's own: "leak:<pattern>", one per line, with
# a comment above each.
#
# --- none yet ------------------------------------------------------------
# The first full run under --asan with detect_leaks=1 is what fills this
# file in: every leak the sanitizer reports is either fixed, reported as
# a finding, or listed here with the reason it is not a leak.
